      "side": 1,
      "message": "With a single descriptor approach, I used to get a failure in flashrom or iteflash. For flashrom, the failure point is here:\n\nhttps://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/third_party/flashrom/raiden_debug_spi.c?rcl\u003db2d845bfa49d65892135c6424d8a927017cea3c5\u0026l\u003d131\n\nAs I understand, libusb_bulk_transfer was expecting data chunk to be delivered with a 1 msec timeout constraint. Meanwhile, if data were located split in CR50 USB tx_q, then CR50 transfers two different time. As I measure, tx_stream_handler() time gap was 4.5 msec or more. \nJust for experiment, I increased the timeout constraint of libusb_bulk_transfer from 1 msec to 10 msec, and it passed, but got failed in another libusb functions. \n\nTo deliver data chunk without timeout violation, two descriptors are needed, I think.",
